# {{ title }}

A Navree microservice, started from the `{{ kit }}` starter kit. It answers
the message `invoices.get`, drafts an invoice when another service publishes
`deal.won`, and publishes `invoice.drafted`, over NATS. Over HTTP it serves
only health checks and metrics.

## Getting started

You need Rust, the `navree` CLI and Docker or Podman.

```sh
navree dock up                 # {{ database_name }} and NATS
navree key:generate            # then set APP_KEY in .env
navree migrate                 # the invoices table
navree dev                     # handlers on NATS, health on http://127.0.0.1:8080/health/ready
```

Try it from another terminal:

```sh
navree micro:patterns
navree micro:emit deal.won '{"deal_id":"0199e5f8-4d0a-7c3e-9a51-3f8f5b6c2d10","amount_cents":129900,"currency":"EUR"}'
```

## What's where

| Path | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `crates/{{ contracts_package }}/` | `GetInvoice`, `Invoice` and the events: what other services depend on |
| `crates/{{ package }}/src/app.rs` | The root: the framework modules, `MicroModule`, the feature modules |
| `crates/{{ package }}/src/modules/invoices/` | The handlers, the service, the model and its migrations |
| `crates/{{ package }}/tests/` | Tests on `MicroFake`'s in-memory transport: no broker needed |

## Calling it from another service

Depend on the contracts crate and send with `ServiceClient`:

```rust
use {{ contracts_crate }}::{GET_INVOICE, GetInvoice, Invoice};

let invoice: Invoice = client.send(GET_INVOICE, &GetInvoice { id }).await?;
```

The caller's bearer token travels with the message, so give every service
the same `auth.jwt.secret` (`APP_AUTH__JWT__SECRET`).

## Another broker

Set `micro.transport` in `config/app.toml` to `kafka`, `rabbitmq`, `redis`,
`mqtt` or `tcp`, and turn on the matching feature (`micro-kafka`, ...) in
`crates/{{ package }}/Cargo.toml`. The handlers stay the same.

